---
import Concept from '../../layouts/Concept.astro';
import Mermaid from '../../components/Mermaid.astro';

const flow = `flowchart TD
  Ready["_ready"] --> Portrait["_setup_portrait"]
  Ready --> Build["_load_shop_items / _generate_*  (build lists)"]
  Build --> Display["_refresh_display"]
  Input["_unhandled_input"] -->|up / down| Sel["_update_selection"]
  Input -->|held| Repeat["_on_nav_repeat"]
  Repeat --> Sel
  Sel --> Display
  Input -->|confirm| Confirm["_open_confirm_modal"]
  Confirm --> Txn["_buy_selected / _sell_selected"]
  Txn --> Mgr["ShopManager.buy_item / sell_item"]
  Mgr --> Display
  Input -->|cancel| Close["close screen"]

  classDef shared fill:#0d1117,stroke:#3fb950,color:#e6edf3,stroke-width:2px
  classDef drift fill:#0d1117,stroke:#d29922,color:#e6edf3,stroke-width:2px
  class Repeat shared
  class Input,Confirm drift
`;
---

<Concept title="Shops" section="Mechanics">
  <div class="diagram"><Mermaid chart={flow} /></div>

  <p>The key words <strong>MUST</strong>, <strong>MUST NOT</strong>, and <strong>MAY</strong> below are used as in RFC 2119.</p>

  <p>Shops are list-driven menus in the city. There are six selling/service counters — <strong>item</strong>, <strong>weapon</strong>, <strong>photon</strong> (units), <strong>tech</strong> (disks), <strong>tekker</strong> (identify/grind), and <strong>crafting</strong> — plus two inventory screens that share the same shell, <strong>storage</strong> (the shared bank) and <strong>equipment</strong>. Each is its own scene under <code>/shop</code>.</p>

  <h2>The shared shopping loop</h2>
  <p>Every counter follows the same shape (the diagram above): on open it builds its lists and draws them, the player navigates a selection with the d-pad (with a hold-to-repeat), <strong>confirm</strong> opens a yes/no (or quantity) modal, and a successful buy/sell runs the transaction and redraws. Currency is the active character's meseta; a purchase <strong>MUST</strong> be rejected if the player can't afford it or has no inventory room, and a successful transaction <strong>MUST</strong> update meseta and inventory before the display refreshes.</p>

  <h2>Counters</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Item</strong> — consumables and materials; bulk-buy aware (quantity dialog). Sell tab buys back inventory.</li>
    <li><strong>Weapon</strong> — weapons by class/requirement; buy/sell with a price-confirm.</li>
    <li><strong>Photon</strong> — units (armor/mag slots).</li>
    <li><strong>Tech</strong> — technique disks; learning is level-gated.</li>
    <li><strong>Tekker</strong> — identify unidentified drops and grind weapons.</li>
    <li><strong>Crafting</strong> — recipes consuming materials.</li>
    <li><strong>Storage</strong> — the shared bank (<code>GameState.shared_storage</code>), cross-character.</li>
    <li><strong>Equipment</strong> — equip/unequip the carried loadout.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Implemented by</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>the six counters under <code>scripts/2d/shops/</code> (<code>item_shop</code>, <code>weapon_shop</code>, <code>photon_shop</code>, <code>tech_shop</code>, <code>tekker</code>, <code>crafting_shop</code>) plus <code>scripts/2d/storage.gd</code> and <code>scripts/2d/equipment_screen.gd</code> — the eight screens (each <code>extends Control</code> today; a shared <code>ShopBase</code> is planned).</li>
    <li><code>scripts/autoloads/shop_manager.gd</code> (ShopManager) — transactions: <code>get_shop_inventory()</code>, <code>buy_item()</code>, <code>sell_item()</code>.</li>
    <li><code>scripts/autoloads/shop_registry.gd</code> (ShopRegistry) — shop definitions / stock (<code>get_shop()</code>, <code>get_all_shops()</code>).</li>
    <li><code>scripts/autoloads/inventory.gd</code> (Inventory) + <code>character_manager.gd</code> (CharacterManager) — the meseta + carried items a transaction reads/writes.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The eight screens share a lot of copy-pasted scaffolding (<code>_get_meseta</code> and <code>_on_nav_repeat</code> are byte-identical across them; <code>_unhandled_input</code> / <code>_open_confirm_modal</code> share a skeleton but have drifted). The de-duplication plan — a <code>ShopBase</code> that owns the shared loop with per-shop override hooks — is tracked in <code>docs/shop-dedup.md</code>.</p>
</Concept>

<style>
  .diagram { margin: 0 0 28px; }
</style>
